  "Description":      "Response and Scene Rendering: renders the machine's response - a Text - with an Avatar, the Model to animate, as a Speaking Avatar ready to play. Text-To-Speech makes the Machine Speech; Generative Face Description and Generative Body Description make the Face and Body Descriptors from the Text and the Machine Speech; when a Personal Status is supplied, Personal Status De-multiplexing splits it into the Speech, Face and Body (Gesture) Personal Statuses that make them expressive, and when it is absent the avatar renders neutrally. Speaking Avatar Synthesis makes the Speaking Avatar. This Implementation produces the Speaking Avatar only; the scene outputs of Scene and Avatar Rendering are not implemented yet.",

